{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["And His saying <b>and I will remember, etc.</b> — meaning, that confession lightens the evil decrees upon them, but to restore them to their nest requires the merit of the fathers, and that is His saying ״וְזָכַרְתִּי״." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say that this is an additional reason for the exile in the land of their enemies, for through this the remembrance of the covenant of the fathers will arise and He will remember them for compassion, which would not have been so otherwise. Also, the remembrance of compassion will come to them when the remembrance of the land is joined with them, and without their exile in the land of the nations there is no need for the remembrance of the land to be remembered along with it. And that is His saying <b>and I will remember,</b> etc., <b>and the land I will remember.</b> And He further added to say <b>and the land shall be left forsaken by them</b> — another reason for the exile, for through this as well the land will be appeased for its Sabbaths, which would not have been so without exile." "<b>My covenant with Jacob, and even et, etc.</b> — meaning, if the merit of Jacob suffices, well and good; and if not, I will add that which is above it, which is the covenant of Isaac; and if that does not suffice, I will join that which precedes it, the covenant of Abraham."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:37.872645279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}